 2. 🚁 Evacuation drone takes flight 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The StarGate drone during a demonstration flight. Photo: Evgeniy Maloletka/AP A Ukrainian brigade is testing a huge drone designed to carry wounded troops to safety.

 The aircraft, developed by Ukrainian defense technology company SkyFall, carries a stretcher underneath six sets of propellers. ⛑️ The drone could quickly reach critically injured soldiers deep in areas under threat of Russian attack.

 AI features and other tech are designed to counter GPS interference now common in Ukraine and other war zones. 💵 The company estimates each system will cost at least $50,000, depending on configuration. It aims to produce up to 1,000 monthly by the end of the year.

